From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:18:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] AROS: per-thread objects behind a pthread key of their
 own

A thread_local object with a destructor is destroyed on AROS after its
storage has been freed: thread_local is GCC's emulated TLS there, whose
storage is released by one pthread key destructor, libstdc++ runs the
thread_local destructors from a key made later, and the pthread library
runs key destructors lowest key first.

SGThreadObject<T> keeps one T per thread behind its own key and deletes
it from that key's destructor. Used for thread_gzPath on AROS.
---
 simgear/io/lowlevel.cxx            |  7 ++++++
 simgear/threads/CMakeLists.txt     |  3 ++-
 simgear/threads/SGThreadObject.hxx | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 simgear/threads/SGThreadObject.hxx

